    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n15007" root="رجو" body-key="r">[
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُرْجٍ</span></b>  and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُرْجِيَةٌ</span> and] <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُرْجِىءٌ</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُرْجِءَةٌ</span> A
female <i>near to bringing forth.</i> (K, * TA.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2- 
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُرْجٍ</span> also signifies A man who is <i>one of the people</i>
[or <i>sect</i>] <i>called the</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُرْجِيَة</span>; (S;) or <i>one of the</i>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُرْجِئَة</span>, mentioned in art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رجأ</span>; as also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُرْجِىءٌ</span>; and
so ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُرْجِىٌّ</span></b> ; (K;) or this is [properly speaking]
a rel. n. from <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُرْجٍ</span>; (S;) and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُرْجِئِىٌّ</span> also; (K;)
or rather this is another rel. n., like <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُرْجِىٌّ</span>. (IB
and TA in art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رجأ</span>, q. v.)

